abstract: >
  QSSI 2026™ (Quantum Sovereign Security Index) is a comprehensive sovereign
  benchmarking, governance analytics, resilience assessment, and research
  infrastructure framework designed to evaluate national preparedness across
  artificial intelligence governance, post-quantum cybersecurity readiness,
  institutional effectiveness, legal and regulatory capacity, economic
  resilience, strategic infrastructure, sovereign security preparedness,
  sustainability, and long-term national capability development.

  The Definitive Master Release v10.0.0 consolidates the complete QSSI
  ecosystem into a unified preservation-grade scholarly resource integrating
  sovereign benchmarking methodologies, computational governance frameworks,
  validation architectures, reproducibility systems, governance registries,
  provenance infrastructures, metadata ecosystems, software transparency
  resources, certification environments, audit mechanisms, FAIR+D preservation
  assets, and long-term scholarly dissemination infrastructure.

  The framework supports evidence-based policy analysis, sovereign benchmarking,
  institutional capacity evaluation, resilience assessment, cybersecurity
  readiness evaluation, governance diagnostics, strategic preparedness
  assessment, computational governance research, and reproducible digital
  scholarship.

